 {"id":"CF-086","title":"16 of 71 board rows embed absolute /home/kara paths, so a reader of this public repo cannot reproduce them — normalize to repo-relative or ~ and refuse new absolute host paths","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:25:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:25:42Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"cdbbf30ec4983b67ced60260135b79640cb0eb57623e6d3bac5427196f4acf75"},"reasoning":"Measured at 532e7b8 with git show HEAD:.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl | grep -c /home/kara = 16 of 71 rows (CF-009 CF-011 CF-012 CF-013 CF-037 CF-045 CF-052 CF-053 CF-055 CF-073 CF-074 CF-076 CF-084 CF-085 PERF-013 PERF-014). This repo is PUBLIC (gh repo view visibility=PUBLIC). Two costs: the rows leak the operator username, and any path the row cites as evidence is unusable off-host — the same reproducibility defect CF-084 files for CF-011/CF-013. Filed by the sync lane 2026-11-03 rather than rewritten in place, because 14 of the 16 rows predate this tick and rewriting evidence text is a separate, reviewable pass.","acceptance_criteria":"A repo check rejects a new or updated board row whose JSON contains an absolute /home/ or /tmp path unless the row names why the path cannot be repo-relative; the 16 rows measured at 532e7b8 are normalized (repo paths repo-relative, out-of-repo paths to ~ with the reason stated); verified by running the check over the committed board with zero findings and bash tests/selftest.sh exiting 0 with the case listed.","capability_tags":["board","public-repo","hygiene"]}
 {"id":"PERF-015","title":"P3 — a foreign commit landed mid-tick and added 6 gate assertions worth 0.345 s CPU (20% of the gate); the 'staged disk floor resolves' row alone is 0.151 s","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:28:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:28:24Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"a25aa570658d8771832d4dc2693a6cbf539b859e255e2c9738cc0bad03875276","evidence":[{"run_id":"code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-16-08-21","ts":"2026-11-03T16:28:24Z"}]},"reasoning":"Measured by the code-factory-perf tick code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-16-08-21 while closing PERF-014. The gate at 400a5ab emitted 34 PASS rows and cost 1.55/1.51/1.49 s user+sys. Commit 77caa02 (CF-075, landed by a sibling lane mid-tick) added section 16 to tests/selftest.sh: six new PASS rows costing, from bash times stamps at 532e7b8, staged disk floor 0.151 s, missing disk floor 0.015 s, manifest validation 0.016 s, owned-failure naming 0.073 s, reused-agent 0.051 s, copy-failure 0.039 s = 0.345 s of a 1.735 s gate. That is three times the 0.09 s cut PERF-014 delivered, and it is the second largest arm in the gate after section 15's 0.524 s of protected documented-command runs. The rows are real assertions, not filler: the question is only whether each needs its own node-create.sh run or can share one staged fixture.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Attribute section 16's six rows individually with a re-runnable script (/usr/bin/time -p, three runs each), not by quoting the foreman's table.\n2. Cut the largest row (staged disk floor resolves, 0.151 s) by a measured amount without losing what it proves: node creation stages every script it executes and resolves the floor from env. Before/after for that arm AND for the whole gate, three consecutive runs each, commands quoted, same tree otherwise.\n3. No assertion dropped, renamed or weakened: the gate keeps 40 PASS rows and SELFTEST: PASS, and the 34 rows present at 400a5ab keep their exact names and counts.\n4. Numbers, commands, per-arm attribution and the honest remaining floor go in docs/audits/code-factory-perf-2026-11-03-PERF-015.md; the commit message names AGENTS.md rule 2 and carries the ch:trace marker for PERF-015.","capability_tags":[]}
 {"id":"CF-087","title":"P3 \u2014 node-create's staged-set validator reads one spelling in two of its four staged files: a ${HERE}/ reference in the entry point and any reference added to the shipped lib.sh print a green --staged-files manifest, so the manifest certifies a node that dies on its first line","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:31:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:31:30Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"qa-lane-readme-2026-11-03-cf087"},"reasoning":"Measured at 9131656 with the row's probe, run from the repo root. Control arm (literal `$HERE/unstaged.py` appended to scripts/project-node.sh): rc=1, `FAIL staged_set \u2014 project-node.sh references unstaged unstaged.py` \u2014 the matcher fires. Braced arm (`${HERE}/unstaged.py` in the same file): rc=0 and the four-line manifest prints, no failure. lib.sh arm (literal `$HERE/unstaged.py` appended to scripts/lib.sh, which ships inside the staged set and is sourced by both the entry point and the adapter): rc=0, four-line manifest, no failure. Cause is visible in scripts/node-create.sh: line 20 keeps a hand-written array `staged=(project-node.sh lib.sh disk_floor.py harness/install-$HARNESS.sh)` and the matcher at line 27 walks only `project-node.sh` and `harness/install-$HARNESS.sh` with pattern `\\$HERE/([a-zA-Z0-9_./$-]+)`, so two of the four staged members are never scanned and the brace form never matches. CF-075 is complete and its AC-1 requires a DERIVED set plus 'a check on the staged set exits nonzero when any referenced file is missing'; that clause does not hold at the closed tip. Filed as a distinct failure mode (validator coverage), not as a duplicate of CF-075 (a member was missing): the 2026-11-03 PERF-014 closure changed tests/test_lane_target.py and the node path, not this validator.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree from the repo root: the `probe` field prints `braced-entry rc=0`, `literal-lib rc=0` and a four-line manifest, and exits 0 today.\n1. `node-create.sh --staged-files` exits nonzero and names the offending file when a runtime reference is added to ANY staged member (at minimum scripts/lib.sh), and when that reference is written as `${HERE}/x`, `$HERE/x` or `'$HERE/x'`; tests/selftest.sh carries one arm per spelling and one arm per staged file, and each arm asserts the NAMED `FAIL staged_set` row (not the substring FAIL, not a traceback).\n2. The staged set is derived rather than hand-listed: the set `--staged-files` prints is computed from the references the shipped scripts actually make, and a member the entry point needs but the set omits cannot pass; either the literal array is gone or it is asserted equal to the derived set.\n3. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip, and reverting the matcher to the two-file, one-spelling form makes the new fixture fail with a named row.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$d/a/harness\" \"$d/b/harness\"; for x in a b; do cp scripts/node-create.sh scripts/project-node.sh scripts/lib.sh scripts/disk_floor.py \"$d/$x/\"; cp scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh \"$d/$x/harness/\"; printf 'X=1\\n' > \"$d/$x/unstaged.py\"; done; printf '\\n. \"${HERE}/unstaged.py\"\\n' >> \"$d/a/project-node.sh\"; printf '\\n. \"$HERE/unstaged.py\"\\n' >> \"$d/b/lib.sh\"; bash \"$d/a/node-create.sh\" --staged-files >\"$d/a.out\" 2>&1; echo \"braced-entry rc=$?\"; bash \"$d/b/node-create.sh\" --staged-files >\"$d/b.out\" 2>&1; echo \"literal-lib rc=$?\"; tail -1 \"$d/a.out\"; tail -1 \"$d/b.out\""}
+{"id": "CF-088", "title": "The selftest board arm accepts any valid JSON, so the gate greens a board that scripts/boardctl validate rejects", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "reasoning": "Measured at 400a5ab by code-factory-releng-qa-2026-11-03-15-39-07. tests/selftest.sh section 7 (\"the board is valid JSONL\") counts a line as a row when json.loads accepts it, and nothing else in the suite runs scripts/boardctl validate against the real board: section 8 exercises only --help and the missing-executable path, and grep -n validate tests/selftest.sh returns one hit that labels a lane-target test. The guard's test_command is bash tests/selftest.sh (no workflows ship), so the validator is never executed by any automated check. The row probe appends six fixtures one at a time to a clone of the tracked board and reads both verdicts: null, [], \"just-a-string\", a duplicate .id and status \"bogus_status\" each print 'PASS 69/69 rows parse / SELFTEST: PASS' while boardctl validate prints '[error] row is not a JSON object', 'duplicate task id', or 'status ... not in vocabulary' and exits 1; a row with no .status slips through both (gate PASS, validator RESULT: OK with a warning), yet such a row is invisible to the selection every foreman uses (.status==\"pending\"). The clean-board control prints 'PASS 68/68 rows parse / SELFTEST: PASS' and 'OK (21 warning(s))'. So the two checks that the repo's own Tier-2 rubric names in the same sentence (\"SELFTEST: PASS and scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK\") disagree on every non-row fixture, and the one wired into the gate is the weaker of the two. Distinct from CF-048 (a truncated final line is skipped before parsing) and CF-069 (the arm dies green when python3 emits nothing: there the arm never runs, here it runs and counts a non-row as a row).", "acceptance_criteria": "1. The selftest board arm fails on a line that is valid JSON but not a JSON object, naming the 1-based line number as boardctl validate does; the row probe's null, array and string fixtures print a gate FAIL instead of 'PASS n/n rows parse'.\n2. A duplicate .id and an out-of-vocabulary .status also fail the gate, either in the arm or by the gate running scripts/boardctl validate against the real board and propagating its exit 1; proven by the probe's duplicate-id and unknown-status arms printing a gate FAIL.\n3. A row with no .status is named as an error (not a warning) by at least one automated check, because such a row is unreachable for select(.status==\"pending\") selection; the probe's missing-status arm must stop reading 'validator: RESULT: OK'.\n4. The negative arms do not depend on boardctl being installed: when the executable is absent the arm either performs the object/duplicate/vocabulary checks itself or fails with the reason named, never a silent pass.\n5. A numbered tests/selftest.sh section covers the clean board as a positive control: it prints '<n>/<n> rows parse' with n equal to wc -l of tasks.jsonl and SELFTEST: PASS at the fixed tip, and the closing evidence shows the same section FAILing on the pre-fix tests/selftest.sh without the fix.\n6. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS, scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK, and the closing commit is pushed with git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD = 0.", "created_at": "2026-11-03T16:36:49Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-03T16:36:49Z", "detail": {"source": "releng-qa", "tick": "code-factory-releng-qa-2026-11-03-15-39-07", "measured_at": "400a5ab"}, "commit_hash": null, "worker_summary": null, "probe": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# probe: the selftest gate's board arm and the shipped validator disagree on every non-row fixture.\n# Run from the root of a code-factory checkout. Writes only inside mktemp; no network.\nset -u\nroot=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) || { echo \"not a git checkout\"; exit 2; }\nt=$(mktemp -d) || exit 2\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$t\"' EXIT\ngit clone -q \"$root\" \"$t/cf\" || { echo \"clone failed\"; exit 2; }\ncd \"$t/cf\" || exit 2\nB=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl\n\ngate()  { bash tests/selftest.sh 2>&1 | grep -E 'rows parse|^SELFTEST' | tr '\\n' ' '; }\nvalid() { if command -v boardctl >/dev/null 2>&1 || [ -x scripts/boardctl ]; then\n            bash scripts/boardctl validate 2>&1 | grep -E '^RESULT|^\\[error\\]' | tr '\\n' ' '\n          else echo \"validator arm SKIPPED (boardctl absent)\"; fi; }\n\narm() { # $1 label, $2 fixture text\n  git checkout -q -- \"$B\"\n  printf '%s\\n' \"$2\" >> \"$B\"\n  printf '%-26s gate: %-38s validator: %s\\n' \"$1\" \"$(gate)\" \"$(valid)\"\n  git checkout -q -- \"$B\"\n}\n\narm \"null-line\"        'null'\narm \"array-line\"       '[]'\narm \"string-line\"      '\"just-a-string\"'\narm \"duplicate-id\"     \"$(git show HEAD:$B | jq -c 'select(.id==\"CF-082\")' | head -1)\"\narm \"unknown-status\"   '{\"id\":\"CF-999\",\"title\":\"bad status\",\"priority\":\"P4\",\"status\":\"bogus_status\"}'\narm \"missing-status\"   '{\"id\":\"CF-900\",\"title\":\"no status\",\"priority\":\"P4\"}'\nprintf '%-26s gate: %-38s validator: %s\\n' \"clean-board(control)\" \"$(gate)\" \"$(valid)\"\ngit checkout -q -- \"$B\"\n"}
